 Rivera"] " from Puerto Rico, and Tulga."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, he met Iranian " [:a {:href "/athletes/155684"} "Rahman Amouzad"] ", the experienced #2 seed and 2022 World champion. Amouzad had defeated American wrestler " [:a {:href "/athletes/155761"} "Zain Retherford"] ", the Albanian " [:a {:href "/athletes/155607"} "Islam Dudaev"] ", and Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/143699"} "Iszmail Muszukajev"] " (the reigning World champion), without conceding a point in all three encounters. This certainly made him a heavy favorite for gold. But Kiyooka had produced a 10-1 lead at the break, and Amouzad only made up two points by a takedown in the second half."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Muszukajev then failed to win bronze, losing by a narrow margin of 13-12 points to Dudaev. Rivera claimed the other bronze, after an equally tight battle by 9-8 points. Both defeated semi-finalists went home without a medal. For the island of Puerto Rico, it was only the second medal in wrestling, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/124748"} "Jaime Espinal"] " in 2012. Dudaev won Albania’s second in any sport, the day after his countryman " [:a {:href "/athletes/155606"} "Chermen Valiev"] " won the first, in the freestyle wrestling 74 kg class."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}